{
  "_readme": [
    "Progression data. Starter decks are the free lists a new account is built from.",
    "One per faction: the faction's starter Leader plus a fixed 30-card list.",
    "The published mix is 17 Common / 9 Rare / 3 Epic / 1 Legendary (economy doc 3.4).",
    "Four factions cannot legally supply 17 Commons - a Leader only has two of the eight",
    "Currents available - so those lists take Rares instead. Every list is 30 cards, legal",
    "for its Leader, and holds exactly 1 Legendary and 3 Epics.",
    "Generated by src/game/progression/starterDecks.ts and frozen here.",
    "THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH: edit a list by hand and the game uses it.",
    "tests/starter-decks.test.ts checks every list is still legal and still buildable.",
    "Any key starting with an underscore is a note and is ignored."
  ],
  "_masteryReadme": [
    "MASTERY. 08-progression.md §4 (Faction Mastery, 20 ranks × 10 factions) and §5",
    "(Leader Mastery, 10 levels × 20 leaders). Both are fed by match XP only: §4 says",
    "'Faction Mastery XP = the match XP (completion + win) you earn while playing that",
    "faction's leader. Missions and bonuses do not count - mastery measures matches",
    "actually played.' The save layer enforces exactly that.",
    "",
    "THE XP-PER-RANK NUMBERS ARE RE-SCALED, AND THE DESIGN SAYS TO DO THIS. §4.1 prints",
    "400/800/1200/1600 per rank, but those are derived from §2.2's assumption that a",
    "match averages 75 XP. The shipped match pays 40 on a win and 25 otherwise - an",
    "average of 32.5 - so the printed numbers would make every track 2.3x longer than",
    "the table's own '~Matches' column, which is the part that expresses the intent.",
    "The doc's preamble settles it: 'If the economy doc diverges, its values win and",
    "reward amounts here are re-scaled.' So the curve below is scaled by 32.5/75 and",
    "rounded to readable numbers, and the MATCH COUNTS are what is preserved:",
    "",
    "  Faction  band 1-5   design ~21 matches   here 700 XP  = 21.5",
    "           band 5-10  design ~53           here 1750    = 53.8",
    "           band 10-15 design ~80           here 2625    = 80.8",
    "           band 15-20 design ~107          here 3500    = 107.7",
    "           TOTAL      design ~261          here 8575    = 263.8",
    "  Leader   band 2-4   design ~12           here 390     = 12.0",
    "           band 5-7   design ~24           here 780     = 24.0",
    "           band 8-10  design ~48           here 1560    = 48.0",
    "           TOTAL      design ~84           here 2730    = 84.0",
    "",
    "tests/mastery.test.ts re-derives that table from `xp` below and fails if anyone",
    "changes match XP without re-scaling the curve - the two cannot drift apart",
    "silently, which is the only way this stays honest.",
    "",
    "REWARD KINDS. `clout`, `fragments` (the game calls this currency Signal),",
    "`pack` (five cards drawn from this faction only), `pick` (choose 1 of N, granted",
    "as `copies` copies) and `lore` are granted for real. `cosmetic` is not: card",
    "backs, portraits, emotes, frames, titles and Premium variants have no system in",
    "the game yet, and granting an invisible reward is worse than not granting it -",
    "the player cannot tell they received it, and it would double-pay once those",
    "screens land and start reading their own state. They are listed here anyway so",
    "the track shows the player what is coming, and mastery.ts refuses to grant them.",
    "See the DEFERRED_COSMETICS allowlist there and its staleness test."
  ],
  "xp": {
    "_note": [
      "What one finished match pays. §2.1 prints 50 + 50; the shipped values are lower",
      "and are the ones every curve in this file is calibrated against. Read by",
      "recordMatch, so the number granted and the number the mastery track is scaled",
      "to cannot come apart."
    ],
    "matchComplete": 25,
    "matchWin": 15
  },
  "checkIn": {
    "_note": [
      "STREAM CHECK-IN - 08 §11. A ten-step track per calendar month. Each day you open",
      "the game claims the NEXT step, and that is the whole rule: no streaks, no resets,",
      "no consecutive-day requirement. Log in on six scattered days and you have six",
      "steps. §10.6.1 makes that binding across the whole game, and this is the one",
      "feature most likely to grow a streak by accident, so it is written down here.",
      "",
      "The track does NOT carry between months (§11), and it does not need to: the",
      "amounts are small and the month-10 cosmetic returns through the Rerun Vault.",
      "Missing a month costs a card back you can get again, which is the difference",
      "between a schedule and a punishment.",
      "",
      "Step 4's reroll tokens are real: missions allow one free reroll per period, and a",
      "token buys another. A token that could not do anything the free reroll cannot",
      "would be a reward in name only."
    ],
